Subject: [PATCH] paymentSource: make isVerifiedSource fail-closed

Remove the legacy `undefined`-means-verified grandfather so ONLY an explicit
status === "verified" routes/backfills/reconciles.

DO NOT MERGE until BOTH are true in EVERY environment (dev + prod):
  1. `npx convex run migrations:backfillPaymentSourceStatus` has been run, AND
  2. its returned {updated} count matches the expected legacy-row count.

Apply as its own commit:
  git apply patches/0001-payment-source-gate-fail-closed.patch
  git commit -am "paymentSource: fail-closed verification gate (post-migration)"
---
diff --git a/convex/lib/paymentSource.ts b/convex/lib/paymentSource.ts
--- a/convex/lib/paymentSource.ts
+++ b/convex/lib/paymentSource.ts
@@ -4,10 +4,9 @@ import type { Doc } from "../_generated/dataModel";
  * A payment source may OBSERVE-route, backfill, and reconcile payments ONLY once
  * its ownership has been verified (see paymentSources.ts verification flow).
  *
- * Legacy rows created before the verification flow have no `status` field and are
- * grandfathered as verified, so the existing (Munchez bootstrap) pipeline keeps
- * working with zero downtime. A migration will set those rows to an explicit
- * "verified". Every NEW row is inserted as "pending" and must be proven first.
+ * Fail-closed: every row now carries an explicit `status` (legacy rows were
+ * stamped "verified" by migrations:backfillPaymentSourceStatus). A "pending" or
+ * "rejected" source — or any row without an explicit "verified" — routes nothing.
  *
  * SECURITY: routing (payments.recordObserved), the orphan backfill, and the
  * clash-guard lock all gate on this — a "pending" or "rejected" source must
@@ -16,5 +15,5 @@ import type { Doc } from "../_generated/dataModel";
 export function isVerifiedSource(
   src: Pick<Doc<"paymentSources">, "status">,
 ): boolean {
-  return src.status === undefined || src.status === "verified";
+  return src.status === "verified";
 }
